<title>USA: Bio-Tech says Biogen appeal dismissed.</title>
<headline>Bio-Tech says Biogen appeal dismissed.</headline>
<dateline>ISELIN, N.J. 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bio-Technology General Corp said Friday an Israeli court has dismissed Biogen Inc's appeal of the Israeli Patents Commissioner's decision to grant a Bio-Technology unit a compulsory license under Biogen's hepatitis-B vaccine patent.</p>
<p>The company said Biogen may still appeal the decision to the Israeli Supreme Court.</p>
<p>In the meantime, the company said the license remains in effect and allows Bio-Technology to register and commercialize its third generation hepatitis-B vaccine in Israel and to export it to countries where Biogen does not have a patent.</p>
</text>
